 for domain renewal and server space may change if ICANN makes a change in their charges or as per the change in Currency rates of Indian Rupees with US Dollars. &nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\nTaxes and Duties: &nbsp;<br />\r\nThe total price for the contract does not include any taxes or other fees payable to the government. If the government in the future levies any tax, fee or other outgoings, the same shall have to be borne by the client.&nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\nI accepted the order amount, and terms &amp;conditions &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;I accepted the order amount, and terms &amp; conditions &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\n1st Party &nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\nThe Secretary/President&nbsp;<br />\r\nCheraman Juma Masjid,&nbsp;<br />\r\nKodungallur, Thrissur<br />\r\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;2nd Party &nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\nHusna M S<br />\r\nPROGRAMERS, Rd North, Thrissur &nbsp;<br />\r\nMob. 9495951442, 9446451442</p>\r\n','',5000,'Social media','INR','Test remarks','Bincy','Bincy',4,0,2,'Husna','2026-12-31','','','','','','','','2026-05-20 11:12:10',NULL,NULL,0,''),(51,'QTN849720052026A',8497,2000,'','',200,'media','inr','','thejas','bdm',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-20 11:59:42',NULL,NULL,0,''),(52,'QTN849720052026B',8497,2000,'','',200,'media','inr','','thejas','bdm',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-20 12:01:20',NULL,NULL,0,''),(53,'QTN849721052026C',8497,0,'','',0,'','','','','',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-21 06:12:16',NULL,NULL,0,''),(54,'QTN849721052026D',8497,1000,'<p>&nbsp;test quatation</p>\r\n','',20,'referal','rupees','nothing','','',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-21 06:16:14',NULL,NULL,0,''),(55,'QTN848521052026C',8485,10000,'<p>SEO vs Google Ads: Which Is Better for Your Business?</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Every business owner in Kerala who&#39;s ever Googled &quot;how to get more customers online&quot; has stumbled into the same crossroads: do you invest in SEO, or do you run Google Ads? Both put your business in front of people who are actively searching. But beyond that, they work in completely different ways &mdash; and picking the wrong one at the wrong time can drain your budget fast.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here&#39;s the honest breakdown.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Key Takeaways</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SEO delivers long-term ROI of up to 1,200% but takes 6&ndash;12 months to see meaningful results (First Page Sage, 2025).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Google Ads can generate leads from week one, but the traffic stops the moment you stop paying.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For most local businesses, the smartest move is to start with Ads for quick wins, then build SEO as your long-term foundation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>What&#39;s the Actual Difference?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SEO (Search Engine Optimisation) is the process of earning a place in Google&#39;s organic search results &mdash; the non-paid links below the ads. It involves optimising your website content, building backlinks, and improving your site&#39;s technical health. When it works, it works for free, indefinitely.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Google Ads is paid placement. You bid on keywords, set a daily budget, and your business appears at the top of results instantly. The moment your budget runs out or you pause the campaign, you disappear.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Think of it this way: SEO is buying land. Google Ads is renting a shop. Both get you customers. But only one keeps giving after you stop paying.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Which One Costs More?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This is where things get interesting &mdash; and a bit counterintuitive.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In India, Google Ads costs between â‚¹10 and â‚¹150 per click depending on your industry, with competitive sectors like real estate and finance pushing CPCs even higher. A modest campaign targeting keywords in Thrissur or Kochi might run â‚¹15,000&ndash;â‚¹30,000 per month once you add agency management fees. That money is gone whether it converts or not.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SEO has upfront costs too &mdash; content writing, technical fixes, link building &mdash; but those investments compound. A page that ranks today can bring in traffic three years from now without an additional rupee spent. Data from home service businesses in 2025 showed that every â‚¹1 spent on SEO returned nearly â‚¹20, while every â‚¹1 on paid ads returned â‚¹4.40. Over a 12-month horizon, that gap widens significantly.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[INTERNAL-LINK: digital marketing ROI for small businesses &rarr; guide on measuring marketing performance]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When Does Google Ads Actually Make Sense?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let&#39;s be fair &mdash; SEO has a real weakness. It&#39;s slow. Most businesses won&#39;t see meaningful organic traffic for six to nine months after starting. If you&#39;ve just launched, have a seasonal offer, or need leads this week, waiting for SEO to kick in isn&#39;t an option.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Google Ads fills that gap. It&#39;s also genuinely powerful for:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Testing offers and messaging before committing to long-form content</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Targeting hyper-specific intent &mdash; someone searching &quot;Thrissur chartered accountant fees&quot; is very close to buying</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Capturing demand during promotional windows like Onam or new product launches</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The catch? You need a healthy enough budget to gather real data &mdash; most experts recommend at least â‚¹10,000&ndash;â‚¹15,000 per month in actual ad spend before conclusions are meaningful.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When Is SEO the Better Bet?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re a local business &mdash; a clinic, a law firm, a restaurant, a digital marketing agency in Kerala &mdash; organic search is where the money is over time. Around 46% of all Google searches have local intent, meaning people are actively looking for businesses near them. Ranking for those searches doesn&#39;t cost â‚¹50 per click. It costs time and the right strategy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>SEO also builds something ads can&#39;t: trust. Users skip paid results more than ever. A business that ranks organically is seen as more credible, especially for high-consideration purchases. A thought leadership SEO campaign, done properly, can deliver a 748% ROI (WordStream, 2026).</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Honest Answer: You Probably Need Both</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Here&#39;s what most marketing consultants won&#39;t say plainly &mdash; the SEO vs Google Ads debate is a bit of a false choice. The businesses seeing the best results in 2026 use Google Ads to generate immediate revenue, then reinvest a portion of that revenue into building SEO that reduces their dependence on paid traffic over time.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Start with Ads if you&#39;re new or need leads now. Build SEO in parallel so that twelve months from now, you&#39;re not paying â‚¹25 per click for traffic you could own for free.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Frequently Asked Questions</p>\r\n\r\n<p>How long does SEO take to show results?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Most businesses start seeing measurable organic traffic improvements between four and nine months after beginning a structured SEO campaign. Competitive industries or new domains take longer. The timeline depends heavily on content quality, backlink strategy, and technical site health.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Is Google Ads worth it for a small business in Kerala?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Yes &mdash; if your average customer value justifies the cost per click. With CPCs averaging â‚¹10&ndash;â‚¹50 in most local service categories, a business where a single customer is worth â‚¹5,000 or more will almost always see positive returns if the campaign is managed well and landing pages are strong.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Can I do SEO and Google Ads at the same time?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Absolutely, and it&#39;s often the recommended approach. Running ads gives you keyword data and conversion insights that directly inform your SEO content strategy. The two channels reinforce each other rather than compete.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Which is better for a local business &mdash; SEO or paid ads?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For long-term growth, local SEO wins. It builds consistent organic visibility in map results and search listings that paid ads can&#39;t replicate. But if you need leads quickly, start with a modest Google Ads campaign while your SEO foundation is being built.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Conclusion</p>\r\n\r\n<p>There&#39;s no single right answer &mdash; but there is a right sequence. Google Ads gets you in the game fast. SEO makes sure you stay in the game without writing a cheque every month.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you&#39;re a business owner in Kerala trying to figure out where your next marketing rupee should go, the answer usually comes down to timeline. Short on time? Start with Ads. Playing the long game? Invest in SEO now so you&#39;re not dependent on ad spend forever.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Want a free audit of your current online visibility? Talk to a digital marketing expert who understands the Kerala market.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n','',100,'gfgsg','inr','hjgxh','ghg','Husna',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-21 07:08:24',NULL,NULL,0,''),(56,'QTN869822052026A',8698,200000,'<p>wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww&#39;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>gddgdhbvsasxbcbhhshghdshgcedgchdghhhhhhhhhhhhhhhgddddddddddddd</p>\r\n\r\n<p>uewyeuuwywuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu</p>\r\n\r\n<p>hhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh</p>\r\n','',2500,'website','rupee','asssss','Amritha','sunitha',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-22 07:00:02',NULL,NULL,0,''),(57,'QTN869822052026B',8698,25000,'<p>A report section in a website is used to present important information in a clear and organized manner for users or administrators. It can include details such as sales data, user activity, project progress, attendance, analytics, or performance summaries. A well-designed website report should contain headings, tables, charts, and brief explanations so that users can easily understand the information. Modern websites often provide downloadable reports in PDF or Excel format and allow filtering by date, category, or user. Reports are commonly used in business websites, school management systems, hospital portals, e-commerce platforms, and admin dashboards to help track records, analyze performance, and support decision-making.</p>\r\n','',1000,'website','rup','','Bincy','sunitha',1,0,0,'','0000-00-00','','','','','','','','2026-05-22 07:33:41','2026-05-22 07:40:43',NULL,0,''),(58,'QTN366329052026A',3663,15500,'<p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus. Donec quam felis, ultricies nec, pellentesque eu, pretium quis, sem. Nulla consequat massa quis enim. Donec pede justo, fringilla vel, aliquet nec, vulputate eget, arcu. In enim justo, rhoncus ut, imperdiet a, venenatis vitae, justo. Nullam dictum felis eu pede mollis pretium. Integer tincidunt. Cras dapibus. Vivamus elementum semper nisi. Aenean vulputate eleifend tellus. Aenean leo ligula, porttitor eu, consequat vitae, eleifend ac, enim. Aliquam lorem ante, dapibus in, viverra quis, feugiat a, tellus. Phasellus viverra nulla ut metus varius laoreet. Quisque rutrum. Aenean imperdiet. Etiam ultricies nisi vel augue. Curabitur ullamcorper ultricies nisi. Nam eget dui. Etiam rhoncus. Maecenas tempus, tellus eget condimentum rhoncus, sem quam semper libero, sit amet adipiscing sem neque sed ipsum. Nam quam nunc, blandit vel, luctus pulvinar, hendrerit id, lorem. Maecenas nec odio et ante tincidunt tempus. Donec vitae sapien ut libero venenatis faucibus. Nullam quis ante. Etiam sit amet orci eget eros faucibu